You want frustrating deaths?  How about being too lucky...

Dr. Utah Jake, Archaeologist, was having a wonderful trip collecting
artifacts for his new museum (ancient parchments, alchemic samples,
primitive jewelry, etc.) when the pangs of hunger started gnawing.

Having too refined a taste to eat raw meat, and frankly not having
much use for the gods other than as an occasional weapon source, he
prayed for food.  This never failed; he did make a point to keep the
gods happy.

But in this case, ol' Quetz was a bit *too* happy.  In addition to
being treated to a filling meal, Dr. J was crowned the Hand of E.

With a deeply shocked cry of "Nooooooo!" and a bitter glance at his
blessed luckstone (he kept the unicorns happy, too, btw), he ditched
his burdensome collectings and sprinted for the stairs, to return to
the storeroom near the surface with his chests of collectings.

Alas, before he attained the level with his box called "Food", the 
hunger once again panged him.  After weakly crawling up another of the 
innumerable flights of stairs, he asked for help.  Quetz was a little
disappointed; after all, he promotes his subordinates so they can go
do things themselves without having to go up the chain so much.

Next, our fainting Hero was crawling on the floor, throwing darts at
a smirking Eye floating nearby (about the only non-friendly beast
about).  His luck served him too well, though, and the Eye was
quickly dispatched, leaving remnants too minute to be consumed.

Finally, as Utah desperately crawled down the last corridor to his
storehouse (more dead than alive), all the beasts who so feared him
when he was able (and who therefore kept their distance), crowded
'round to tease him in his last moments.  But he kept them at bay,
until at last he was greeted with a vision, "Do you want to see...."

Dr. Utah Jake, Archaeologist: starved to death.

